Spotted via analyze_tool_costs.py — a throwaway script that ranks
tool calls in session transcripts by word count. The git log result
showed up at rank 3 (~1500 words) when it should have cost maybe 50.

The grep -v "Merge tag" filter was also fragile: it kept internal
sub-branch merges (e.g. "Merge branch 'topic/foo' into wip/bar")
visible alongside regular commits, which is neither a clean
non-merge list nor a topology-only view. The prescribed form splits
these two questions with --no-merges and --merges respectively.

